ight durban's  different communities  are still closing themselves in behind  their own checkpoints there are outside  elements that are coming here  and get very upset when we have to ask  them what is your purpose here  people here are worried there's more  trouble to come  it's not quite it's not settling down  there's areas that no one's focusing on  and that's the concern  there are areas which are every day  there's blue team burning still  continuing  and no one sees that just hours after  south africa's president said on friday  night  that calm had been restored this market  was firebombed bernard smith al-jazeera  durbin south africa
 

